# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Wallpapers (add your own, don't commit large binaries)
# wallpapers/Pictures/Wallpapers/*.jpg
# wallpapers/Pictures/Wallpapers/*.jpeg
# wallpapers/Pictures/Wallpapers/*.png
# wallpapers/Pictures/Wallpapers/*.webp
# !wallpapers/Pictures/Wallpapers/.gitkeep

# Theme engine runtime output (PIPE-03/D-05) — generated colors live in
# ~/.local/state/theme/, outside this repo. Two consumers have no native
# @import/include mechanism (walker, yazi, D-07) so theme-engine wires their
# config path directly with a symlink into the state dir; since both live
# under whole-package stow symlinks back into this repo tree, the symlink
# theme-apply creates lands at these exact repo-relative paths — ignore it.
walker/.config/walker/themes/rice/style.css
yazi/.config/yazi/theme.toml

# Wallpaper runtime pointer (D-23) — `current.jpg` is a relative symlink
# rewritten on every static theme switch by lib/wallpaper.sh's `ln -sfr`,
# by wallpaper-picker.sh, and by a file-manager action; read by the
# Material You generator (generate.sh) and the lock screen
# (hyprlock.conf). Committing it made a runtime pointer look like repo
# content and permanently dirtied the tree on any non-default static
# theme, which is why the fix here is to untrack it rather than exempt
# the clean-tree check from it. Seeded at install time by stow.sh instead
# of tracked, so a fresh install still lands on the same wallpaper.
wallpapers/Pictures/Wallpapers/current.jpg

# Screenshots (D-48) — runtime output from screenshot.sh, never repo content.
# Belt-and-suspenders alongside the .stow-local-ignore fold exclusion above.
wallpapers/Pictures/Screenshots/

# GSD research cache — ephemeral web-research cache written by the research
# skill/tool, never meant to be tracked (CLEAN-02/D-50 git-clean invariant).
.planning/research/.cache/

# container-run.sh runtime logs (03-04) — machine-readable evidence written
# per invocation under verify/logs/run-<timestamp>/, never repo content.
verify/logs/

# AGS generated GObject-introspection TypeScript defs (10-05) — `ags types`
# regenerates this on demand from whatever GI typelibs are installed on the
# machine; equivalent to a node_modules/@types cache, never repo content.
ags/.config/ags/@girs/

# Desktop entries (stow-symlink side effect). vscodium/.local/share/applications/
# is stow-symlinked to ~/.local/share/applications/, so any app that registers a
# launcher (Steam, Lutris, installers) writes its .desktop straight into this repo
# and trips theme-doctor's clean-tree gate. Ignore by default; the entries we
# deliberately version are opted back in below.
vscodium/.local/share/applications/*
!vscodium/.local/share/applications/codium.desktop
!vscodium/.local/share/applications/claude-code-url-handler.desktop
